[
    {
        "content": "<p>Have monoid homomorphisms between monoid objects been defined on Mathlib? Somthing like,</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Monoidal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Cartesian</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Mon</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CartesianMonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonObj</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CartesianMonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonObjHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">hom_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">η</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">η</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">hom_mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗ₘ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hom</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>When I asked Claude AI, it said that it could not find it.</p>\n<p>I want to use the fact that the for a group object, the endomorphisms form a ring.</p>",
        "id": 621435616,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788450609
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.IsMonHom#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.IsMonHom</a></p>",
        "id": 621450386,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1788453711
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, thanks. But, this is class. Unlike standard algebraic structures, can we not bundle all the homomorphisms together? Something like,</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonObjHom'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonObj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">is_monoid_morphism</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMonHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If not, is there a reason something like this does not exist?</p>",
        "id": 621452714,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788454227
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Mon.ofHom#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Mon.ofHom</a> which takes the <code>IsMonHom</code> instance implicitly and gives you a bundled morphism between <code>Mon.mk G ⟶ Mon.mk H</code></p>",
        "id": 621455446,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1788454810
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Cool! Thanks.</p>",
        "id": 621455921,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788454907
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This isn't precisely what I am looking for. I am look for a structure <code>MonHom G H</code> such that any term of that structure is a monoid homomorphism. It shouldn't be a problem to construct. But, I feel like it's not there on Mathlib, and I was wondering why</p>",
        "id": 621457970,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788455342
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is it not <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Mon.Hom#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Mon.Hom</a> ? That's the result type of <code>Mon.ofHom</code></p>",
        "id": 621463633,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1788456593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You have <code>(G : C) [MonObj G] (H : C) [MonObj H]</code>, and <code>Mon.Hom</code> is just the uncurried version, which takes <code>(M N : Mon C)</code>, where <code>Mon C := (X : C) × MonObj X</code></p>",
        "id": 621465332,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1788456903
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ahh, silly me. Found it. Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 621465562,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1788456952
    }
]